<title>USA: Union Carbide Corp Q3 net shrinks.</title>
<headline>Union Carbide Corp Q3 net shrinks.</headline>
<dateline>DANBURY, Conn. 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call mean estimate for Q3 was $1.10 per share</p>
<p>							Quarter Ended</p>
<p>					    Sep 30,	   Sep 30,</p>
<p> Millions of Dollars, Except Per	 1996	   1995</p>
<p>Share Amounts</p>
<p> NET SALES				  $ 1,538	  $1,495</p>
<p> NET INCOME				     161	     277</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>   Primary				     1.19	    1.96</p>
<p>Based on the indicated number  </p>
<p>	 of shares		    133,436,084   140,324,041</p>
<p>   Fully diluted			     1.08	    1.77</p>
<p>Based on the indicated number</p>
<p>	 of shares		    149,781,685    156,874,871</p>
<p>					    Nine Months Ended Sept. 30,</p>
<p> Millions of Dollars, Except Per		1996	  1995</p>
<p>Share Amounts</p>
<p> NET SALES					 $ 4,598	$ 4,489</p>
<p> NET INCOME					    491	    735</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>   Primary					    3.52	   5.11</p>
<p>Based on the indicated number</p>
<p>	 of shares			   136,875,350  142,086,594</p>
<p>   Fully diluted				    3.20	   4.61</p>
<p>Based on the indicated number</p>
<p>	 of shares			   153,167,288  159,223,673</p>
<p>NOTE - Q3 1995 figures include a gain of $161 million, or $0.32 per share, from the sale of its remaining interests in UCAR International Inc, and a $68 million charge for postemployment benefits, including severance.</p>
<p>Figures for the first nine months of 1995 include a $381 million gain from the sale of its remaining interests in UCAR International Inc, and a $191 million charge for future lease payments on unused office space primarily at the company's Danbury headquarters.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
